add('DP-04','Your Features, Two Bold Inks','your-features-two-bold-inks-profile','Profile Picture',
 'Create a simplified two-ink linocut portrait in dark indigo and burnt orange on warm off-white stock. Use broad carved shapes that follow the reference person’s actual eyes, nose, lips, cheek structure and facial hair. Keep the eyes and mouth resolved as recognizable features, not generic decorative symbols. Preserve glasses frames, hairline, beard outline and age cues where present. Allow only sparse paper grain outside facial landmarks; no dense halftone over the eyes. A plain off-white ground and one small flat shoulder shadow are enough. No train window, scenery, lettering, poster layout or period costume. This is one centred avatar, not a crop from a multi-element poster.',
 'A personal graphic avatar with the clarity of an icon and the character of a print.',
 'Reinterprets an individual face as controlled printmaking while retaining its landmark relationships.',
 'Use the approved fictional Indian adult man in the supplied PicMagic identity fixture: preserve his curly hair, beard, recognizable geometry, apparent age and natural proportions; translate tones into indigo and burnt-orange inks.',
 'High: over-simplification can replace the reference with a generic face. Reject if recognizability fails at 64px or features shift in paired comparison.',
 'An intentionally separate square profile composition from the existing railway-print post: different framing, broad marks, no setting and no costume/era transformation. Shares a useful medium, not a duplicated asset or source composition.', ['AP03','CG04'],art=True,refs=['docs/audits/creative-batch-2026-09-11/sources/p02-identity-fixture.png'])
add('DP-05','A Cameo Made of Clay','cameo-made-of-clay-profile','Profile Picture',
 'Translate the supplied head-and-shoulders portrait into a warm terracotta bas-relief with one recognizable face emerging gently from a plain darker clay backing. Retain the person’s specific facial geometry, wrinkles, hairline, cheek marks and glasses or facial hair where supplied. Use broad shallow relief and soft light from above-left to make the eyes, nose and mouth readable; avoid deep black eye sockets, a blank mask or idealized classical anatomy. Keep material colour consistently terracotta; it represents clay, not a replacement complexion or ethnicity. Preserve relative tonal structure through modelling and shadow. Do not show a pedestal, museum room, lettering, fragmented body or a second face.',
 'A distinctive personal keepsake-style avatar that reads as one face at small size.',
 'Creates a convincing custom sculpted likeness without commissioning and photographing a physical relief.',
 'Use the approved fictional Indian older woman in the supplied PicMagic portrait fixture; preserve her short silver-grey hair shape, age lines, cheek mark, facial geometry and ordinary proportions in terracotta relief. Do not rejuvenate her.',
 'High: sculpture can erase individuality and age cues; reject deep eye shadows or a generic classical face. This is the first concept to drop if small-size recognizability fails.',
 'Sculpted shallow clay with continuous modelling, not the existing layered paper portrait, an enamel travel badge or a stock marble bust.', ['CG01','CG06'],art=True,refs=['docs/audits/creative-batch-2026-09-11/sources/p13-portrait-fixture.png'])
